/**
 * Owns unsupported Java 26 Class-File generation from canonical CPU kernel IR.
 *
 * <p>Emitters consume an already-selected exact scalar specialization and generate one universal
 * primitive {@code start}/{@code end} loop over its exact ordered {@code double[]} or
 * {@code MemorySegment} carrier pattern. The selected access regime shapes a primitive dense,
 * constant, last-axis, block/outer, or general-odometer state machine. Emitters do not inspect
 * graph nodes, choose numerical policy, select a route, bind runtime resources, or persist
 * artifacts. Generated bytes are verified before definition and are handed to the cache and
 * executable packages as strongly owned immutable artifact state.
 *
 * <p>Generation and verification are cold-path operations. Only the resolved static entry handle
 * executes on the Runtime hot path.
 */
